course: dictionary
lesson: 5246
title: Job and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word job has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one. «Her job is a nurse» means the work she does to earn money. «My job is to feed the cat» means a task or piece of work, even though nobody pays you to feed the cat.
explain: Read the clues. If someone says «Good job!», they are not talking about money at all. They mean well done. «Do the job» means work well enough to get it finished, and «a part-time job» means fewer hours than a full-time one.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Put "work someone does to earn money" into «In Swansea, Saffie's mam works two jobs» and it still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A job is work someone does to earn money.
fact: A job can also be a task or piece of work, such as a chore at home.
fact: «Good job!» means well done.
fact: «Odd jobs» are small, different tasks, such as jobs around the house or garden.
fact: «Some high-paying jobs need long hours»: £60,000 a year is £5,000 a month, because £60,000 ÷ 12 = £5,000.
exercise: «Her job is a nurse.» What does job mean here? | A bag she carries to school | A game she plays with friends | *The work she does to earn money | A song she likes
exercise: «Good job!» What does it mean? | It is time for lunch | Please leave the room now | *Well done | You have broken something
exercise: «In Swansea, Saffie's mam works two jobs.» What does jobs mean? | Two new houses | *Paid work she does to earn money | Two sad days | A pile of old paper
test: «My job is to feed the cat.» What kind of job is this? | A type of cat food | Work done to earn money | *A task or piece of work | A holiday
test: Dad says, «Just do the job, it doesn't need to be perfect.» What does do the job mean? | Give up and do nothing | *Work well enough to get it finished | Stop at once and go to bed | Do it perfectly, with no mistakes
exam: Which meaning fits «Some high-paying jobs need long hours»? | Chores done at home | Small jobs done in the garden | Things people say to show well done | *Work people do to earn money
